# The second half of `save.rec`'s round trip, and the reason a session
# library needs more than one starting disk: this one begins from the
# directory that session ended with — a slot A holding a saved party.
#
# The file and dir lines are a snapshot of that directory: names, sizes
# and SHA-256s, written by `scripts/sweep.py --pin`. No byte of the
# player's installation is here (CONTRIBUTING.md).

about boot through the code-wheel challenge to LOAD SAVED GAME, slot A,
about and the party back where it was saved — 0,4 W, the same character,
about the same AC and the same hit points, on the exploration bar
disk external

